From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] a dma-buf a driver imports only as memory the heap's properties do not name is imported as that memory

accel-virt: NVIDIA lists the system memory types it can import a foreign dma-buf as, and imports into them one with no host-visible bit while refusing the host-visible types the heap names. The pages are mapped by the caller, so the memory type does not have to be host visible: after the types of the heap, every type the buffer lists is tried, which the swap chain heaps of a render-only adapter needed.
---
diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/memory.c b/libs/vkd3d/memory.c
index 73d6b5a..2f4aa06 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/memory.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/memory.c
@@ -1284,6 +1284,15 @@ static HRESULT vkd3d_import_fd_memory(struct d3d12_device *device, int fd,
             return hr;
     }
 
+    untried = fd_properties.memoryTypeBits & ~type_mask & ((1u << device->memory_properties.memoryTypeCount) - 1u);
+    while (untried)
+    {
+        uint32_t type_index = vkd3d_bitmask_iter32(&untried);
+
+        if (SUCCEEDED(hr = vkd3d_import_fd_attempt(device, fd, size, 0, 1u << type_index, pNext, allocation)))
+            return hr;
+    }
+
     WARN("Failed to import dma-buf memory, hr %#x, memory types %#x of %#x.\n",
             hr, fd_properties.memoryTypeBits, type_mask);
     return hr;
